Every year since 2014, [[PONOS Corporation]] has set up pranks for April Fools' Day, most of which involve fake articles.

==List of Jokes==
===2014===
*PONOS posted an [http://www.ponos.co.jp/pc/newspaper/20140401.html article] about a [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] who is suspected of not actually being a cat after entering the real world.

===2015===
*PONOS posted an [http://www.ponos.co.jp/pc/newspaper/20150401.html article] with an image edited to have giant [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]] statue next to the Statue of Liberty, built to celebrate the release of [[The Battle Cats POP!]]. It also states that there are plans to build a similar statue of [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] in the city for which she is named.

===2016===
*[[Let's Start Over]] was replaced with an easier version of [[Love and Death]].
*PONOS posted an [http://ponos.co.jp/pc/newspaper/20160401.html article] announcing the success of the [[Battle Items#Cat CPU|Cat CPU]]'s newly improved AI, along with plans to use it in real-world applications. Other subjects include a partership with the [[wikipedia:West Japan Railway Company|West Japan Railway Company]] to create a [[Nyanko Daisensou]] themed card to spend [[Cat Food]] on train rides and earn points for purchasing [[Cat Units]] with, as well as the announcement of a new magazine detailing the history and inner workings of the [[Cat Base]]. Each issue would come with a part for the subscriber to build their very own version of it.

===2017===
*All [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] from [[Into the Future]] Chapters 2 and 3 had their effects removed.
*PONOS posted an [https://ponos.s3.amazonaws.com/information/appli/battlecats/aprilfool/2017/index_en.html article] announcing on the discovery of the [[:Category:Li'l Cats|Li'l Cats]]' [[True Form]]s, which were still unknown to players at the time.

===2018===
*PONOS posted an [https://ponos.s3.amazonaws.com/information/appli/battlecats/aprilfool/2018/index_en.html article] about a made-up game called "School Cat Club Idol Heart Live Plus!", a parody of the mobile rhythm game series ''Love Live! School Idol Festival''.
**The right-hand side of the article includes an advertisement for "Your Cat's Name"; a parody of ''Your Name''; underneath the ad, there are headlines that mention Anyazon, Instantgram and DogeTube, parodying Amazon, Instagram and YouTube, respectively.

===2019===
*PONOS posted an [https://ponosgames.com/information/appli/battlecats/aprilfool/2019/index.html article] about a made-up game called "In [[wikipedia:Shōwa (1926–1989)|Shōwa]]! Nyanko Great War", a 4-bit game released on the Family Nyamputer. This game's continuation feature, which lets players resume play using a password, is touted as revolutionary.

===2020===
*Players received 1 XP as a [[Daily Bonus|stamp reward]].
*PONOS posted an [https://ponosgames.com/information/appli/battlecats/aprilfool/2020/index.html article] about an electronic pay service called "NyanPay", which allows you to make transactions by holding a [[wikipedia:Koban (coin)|koban]] to the cash register, and a large-scale cash back campaign to raise 222.2 billion yen.

===2021===
*PONOS posted an [https://battlecats.club/special/aprilfool/2021/ article] about the release of real-life AI [[Catway (Super Rare Cat)|Drone Cats]], which are touted as being capable of delivering packages within 22 minutes of an order being placed.

===2022===
*PONOS posted an [https://battlecats.club/special/aprilfool/2022/ article] about the release of a Battle Cats themed area at [[wikipedia:Universal Studios Japan|Universal Studios Japan]], which would feature all sorts of attractions related to the main game.

===2023===
*Players received 1 [[Cat Capsule|Cat Ticket]].
*PONOS posted an [https://battlecats.club/special/aprilfool/2023/ article] about a movie adaptation on the mobile game with the release date of February 22nd, 2222.

===2024===
*Players received 1 [[Cat Capsule|Cat Ticket]].
*PONOS posted an [https://battlecats.club/special/aprilfool/2024/ article] about a parody of [[wikipedia:The Bachelor (American TV series)|The Bachelor]], with [[The Cat God (Special Cat)|Cat God]] being the titular bachelor.

===2025===
*Players received 1 [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Ticket]].
*PONOS posted an [https://battlecats.club/special/aprilfool/2025/ article] about a parody of [[wikipedia:Sega Saturn|Sega Saturn]], which is slated for release on February 22nd, 2222.

===2026===
*Players received 1 [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Ticket]].
*PONOS posted an [https://battlecats.club/special/aprilfool/2026/ article] announcing the release of an anime adaptation of The Battle Cats supposedly featuring a blazing fast 1 frame per second.

